Subject: cairo-program-runner-lib: keep the privacy bootloader output preimage in the execution scopes; make the file dump optional

Why (Hellproof S2, wasm64): `dump_privacy_simple_bootloader_output_preimage` is the only hint of
the leaf simple bootloader that touches the filesystem (`std::fs::write` of the output preimage).
`wasm64-unknown-unknown` has no filesystem, so the leaf bootloader cannot run in the browser
without this change. The preimage is now always inserted into the execution scopes under
`output_preimage` (readable by the caller through `CairoRunner::exec_scopes`), and the file is
written only when `output_preimage_dump_path` is non-empty. Existing callers (privacy_prove,
stwo_run_and_prove_recursive_tree tests, leaf_prover) pass a real path and are unaffected.

Upstream: to be submitted as a PR against starkware-libs/proving (base cd7bc5f).

--- a/crates/cairo-program-runner-lib/src/hints/privacy_simple_bootloader_hints.rs
+++ b/crates/cairo-program-runner-lib/src/hints/privacy_simple_bootloader_hints.rs
@@ -42,6 +42,13 @@
         vm.get_integer_range(output_start, size)?.into_iter().map(|v| v.into_owned()).collect();
 
     let dump_path: PathBuf = exec_scopes.get(vars::OUTPUT_PREIMAGE_DUMP_PATH)?;
+    // Always keep the preimage in the execution scopes so that callers without a filesystem
+    // (wasm) can read it back through `CairoRunner::exec_scopes`; dump it to a file only when a
+    // path was given.
+    exec_scopes.insert_value(vars::OUTPUT_PREIMAGE, elements.clone());
+    if dump_path.as_os_str().is_empty() {
+        return Ok(());
+    }
     let json = serde_json::to_string_pretty(&elements).map_err(|e| {
         HintError::CustomHint(format!("Failed to serialize output preimage: {e}").into())
     })?;
--- a/crates/cairo-program-runner-lib/src/hints/vars.rs
+++ b/crates/cairo-program-runner-lib/src/hints/vars.rs
@@ -75,3 +75,6 @@
 
 /// Path to dump the output preimage for privacy simple bootloader.
 pub const OUTPUT_PREIMAGE_DUMP_PATH: &str = "output_preimage_dump_path";
+
+/// The privacy simple bootloader output preimage (`Vec<Felt>`), kept in the execution scopes.
+pub const OUTPUT_PREIMAGE: &str = "output_preimage";
